Yep, after years of sucky playing I finally got my reward today.
Judging by my recent games, I knew I'd finally achieved the skills
required to complete NetHack, and that if I only could quit making
stupid mistakes, I'd probably ascend soon. A recent Healer died on the
Astral Plane due to inexperience on the endgame, and a Samurai ready
for an ascension run ended up quitting after losing most of his stuff
because of a drunken mistake of mine. (I put a back of tricks inside a
BoH, KABLAMM!)  This time I wanted to try a Wizard, partly because
they often get cool items in their starting inventory and partly
because I hadn't played one in a while.

I was lucky enough to start out with a ring of teleport control, a
magic marker, a wand of speed monster and and a spellbook of magic
missile. The cat died an early death, so I couldn't do the protection
racket. The stair to the Mines was on level 2, and I headed right
there. Found a magic lamp along the way. I didn't proceed past the
town yet, since my AC sucked and I was getting beaten rather badly
already. The altar in the Town was co-aligned, so upon having enough
HP to withstand an artifact blast I blessed the lamp and wished for
the Staff of Aesculapius. Went back to the main dungeon and started
working my way down. Enchanted the Staff to +7 and advanced
quarterstaff to Expert. Found a +4 pair of leather gloves and a pair
of speed boots rather quickly, and also added a studded leather armor
and an elven leather helm. Had no real problems mapping out the
dungeon down to Medusa's island. At some point I stopped to utilize my
Create Monster spell and sacrifice a lot. I got a whole bunch of
artifacts: Magicbane, Mojo, Ogresmasher, Cleaver, Trollsbane and
Dragonbane, IIRC.  Magicbane became my backup weapon and I advanced it
to Basic. The other artifacts I left behind. 

After killing Medusa I went back to do Sokoban. Got a BoH. I still
wasn't XP 14, so I headed out for the castle after wiping out the L.
Slayed a silver dragon at the closets near the storage rooms and
enchanted its scales. The wishes went for two more candles (Izchak's
shop only had five), spellbooks of finger of death, cone of cold,
identify and magic mapping. Now at XP 15, I went on the Quest. Dark
One was surprisingly wimpy (hadn't done the Wiz quest before). Three
hits of Staff was enough to send him in. He cursed some of my items
though, but I didn't worry about that too much, as I knew the spell
Remove Curse and was Skilled at divination spells. Next up was the
snoozefest known as Gehennom. I found some scrolls of genocide and
enchant armor on the first few levels, and got rid of the R and the h,
plus made all armor fooproof and +4 / +5. On the whole, not much
happened in Gehennom. I kept on casting magic mapping and digging
until I reached the bottom. Never bothered to properly explore the
levels, since I pretty much already had all I needed, save for a ring
of free action maybe. Marked the vibrating square, then invoked the
Eye to open a portal to the Mines, and went back to get the luckstone.
Returned to Gehennom, killed Rodney and the high priest, grabbed the
Amulet and ran back to dlvl 1. The "mysterious force" thingy was very
annoying, and the journey back seemed to take forever. I insta-killed
Rodney with finger of death whenever he appeared. One time an urge of
beating him in a "fair fight" took me over, but after three turns of
melee I reverted to my insta-kill strategy. As I had never ascended
before, I wanted to play it safe.

So I entered the Planes. Earth was easy, as the portal was quite close
to my starting location. Air was tough as I expected. Ring of
conflict, finger of death and a wand of polymorph helped a lot,
though. Didn't have free action but thanks to conflict, I wasn't
threatened too badly when paralyzed, since the monsters were fighting
each other. Fire was a real clusterf**k. I had already used up the two
gold detection scrolls that I had, so  I had to patiently search for
the portal. At some stage, an Archon showed up and started summoning
nasties (including other Archons.) Soon there was six Archons and
shitloads of monsters on the level. For the first time in the game I
seriously thought I was going to die, but conflict saved my ass again.
I made taking out the Archons my priority, and left the other monsters
to battle each other. Eventually the portal was found. I expected
Water to take an eternity, but this time it was over after 30 turns or
so. The bubbles merged almost right away, revealing the location of
the portal.

I proceeded to the Astral Plane. Me and the Angel started moving to
the rightmost altar. I chose to fight, and to save the only wand of
teleportation I had for later use. Famine went down smoothly with the
finger of death. The hordes of monsters were too much for the Angel,
who died before reaching the first altar. I arrived to the temple.
Lawful. Set out for the temple at the center, guarded by Death. Before
I could even notice, he was standing next to me. My first plan was to
kill him in melee, but as my max HPs kept on dropping, I retreated
back and started blasting him with wands from a distance. Death
started to flee, and I realized this was my chance. I rushed to the
temple, teleporting stuff outta my way, hoping the altar would be the
Neutral one. And it was! I offered the Amulet of Yendor to Thoth...
The invisible choir sang, and I was bathed in radiance... YAY!

